# Operator config

**Skill:** `.cursor/skills/operator-config/SKILL.md` (MUST Read and follow when this rule loads). Patterns: that skill's `reference.md`.

## MUST

- Put live operator config under `~/.config/<app>/` (or `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/<app>/`)
- Prefer `<APP>_CONFIG` / `--config`, then user `config.yaml`, then documented cwd fallbacks
- Provide `make init` / `<bin> init` that creates user config if missing (`0600`)
- Keep secrets out of YAML literals; use `${VAR}` and/or Keychain account names
- Resolve runtime secrets env-first, then optional Keychain; fail closed when required and empty

## MUST NOT

- Ship cwd-only config discovery with no user-dir candidate
- Overwrite existing user `config.yaml` without an explicit force flag
- Commit literal API keys, passwords, tokens, or credential URLs in config examples
- Require macOS Keychain on Linux/CI as the only secret source
- Conflate license signing-key Keychain items with app password Keychain items
